From d00f20c7b973c73de46c51948bb995bc46925c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deliveroo Backend <dev@deliveroo.local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 05:54:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Add real Google Maps geocoding and routing providers

Geocoding and routing have been running on fixed stub data this whole
time (every address geocodes to the same point in Nairobi, every route
is a flat 10km/25min) - fine for tests, but not something you can ship
real distances or map markers from.

- Add GoogleGeocodingService (Geocoding API) and GoogleRoutingService
  (Directions API), selected via GEOCODING_PROVIDER=google and
  ROUTING_PROVIDER=google respectively - same toggle pattern already
  used for notifications
- Both fail soft: a missing API key, a bad address, or a network error
  all return None rather than raising, since the calling code already
  treats a failed geocode/route as non-fatal
- Add GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY setting (server-side key, separate from the
  frontend's browser-restricted VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY - needs
  Geocoding API and Directions API enabled, and should be IP-restricted
  rather than referrer-restricted)
- Add requests to requirements.txt
- Document all of the above in .env.example
- Add tests against mocked HTTP responses so the parsing logic is
  covered without needing real network access or a live API key

Defaults stay on the stub providers, so nothing changes for local dev
or CI until GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY and the provider toggles are actually
set.
